an empty manifest is a valid container
a well-formed row parses
a row's triples are preserved verbatim
an unknown triple is refused
an empty triples list is refused
a missing required field is refused
a blank required field is refused
malformed TOML is refused
a non-array `engine` key is refused
an `engine` entry that is not a table is refused
a non-array `corroboration_urls` is refused
a PREBUILT row without asset_sha256 is refused - there is nothing to verify against
the group tokens default to the row's own id/version
a declared group token overrides the default
the cache key is `<cache_engine>-<cache_version>-<triple>`
an undeclared group falls back to the row key
a DECLARED-but-blank group token is refused rather than silently defaulted
a cache token that is not one path component is refused: '../evil'
a cache token that is not one path component is refused: 'a/b'
a cache token that is not one path component is refused: 'a\\b'
a cache token that is not one path component is refused: '.hidden'
a cache token that is not one path component is refused: ''
a cache token that is not one path component is refused: '  '
the cache_VERSION half of the grammar is checked too, not only cache_engine
a DEFAULTED token is checked too - the id is the fallback, so it is a path component
an ordinary versioned token passes the grammar
a prebuilt staged artifact is fetchable
a from-source row is NOT fetchable
a sub-component row is NOT fetchable
the from-source refusal names P4.28.1's compile path
the sub-component refusal names the row KIND, not the acquisition mode
an explicit valid triple resolves to itself
an unknown explicit triple is a structural error
this host resolves to a v1 triple, or says plainly that it cannot
an IMPLICIT target resolves like the host table says, or refuses in so many words
every mapped host triple is a declared v1 triple
an https URL is accepted
the scheme pin refuses file://
the scheme pin refuses http://
the scheme pin refuses ftp://
a hostless URL is refused
an off-allow-list host is refused even over https
an allow-listed host passes
the REAL opener carries the guard itself, not its caller
the REAL opener refuses an off-allow-list host before opening a socket
every redirect hop is re-checked - the handler refuses a downgrade to http
every redirect hop is re-checked - the handler refuses a cross-origin hop
the per-hop pin is INSTALLED on the opener the fetch actually uses
the STREAMING ceiling refuses mid-read, before the whole body is buffered
an oversized download is refused after the fact too, by fetch_asset's own bound
a body under the ceiling reads back whole
a multi-chunk payload reads back in ORDER, not as a repeated prefix
an empty download is refused
a transport failure is reported as a fetch violation, not a traceback
a matching digest verifies
an UPPERCASE pin still verifies
a mismatching digest is refused, as a MISMATCH
a short pin is refused as MALFORMED, not as a mismatch
a non-hex pin is refused as MALFORMED, not as a mismatch
a 64-char pin of the WRONG bytes still reads as a mismatch
a plain member is confined
a hostile member path is refused: '/etc/passwd'
a hostile member path is refused: '../escape'
a hostile member path is refused: 'a/../../escape'
a hostile member path is refused: 'C:evil'
a hostile member path is refused: '\\\\host\\share'
a hostile member path is refused: ''
an interior-NUL member is refused
a backslash-spelled traversal is refused
tar magic wins over a wrong name
zip magic wins over a wrong name
a bare payload is raw
an empty-zip EOCD magic is recognised
a .zip NAME is the fallback when the bytes do not decide
a .tar.gz NAME is the fallback when the bytes do not decide
a .tgz NAME is the fallback too
a tar unpacks as a tree
a zip unpacks as a tree
a bare binary is stored under its own name
a bare-asset NAME that escapes the entry root is refused AS a member violation
a separator in a bare-asset name is refused CLEANLY, or lands flat in the entry
a dot bare-asset name is refused too
the stdlib data filter is applied - a device-node member is refused
a truncated tar container is a violation, not a traceback
a truncated zip container is a violation, not a traceback
a traversing TAR member is refused AS a traversal, before extraction
a traversing TAR SYMLINK target is refused AS a traversal
a traversing ZIP member is refused AS a traversal, before extraction
the refused traversal wrote NOTHING outside the entry
an archive that unpacks to nothing is refused
three rows of one entry collapse into ONE plan
the plan names every member it carries
the group is NOT keyed on the row's own version
a group whose members disagree on the entry hash fails closed
a group whose members disagree on the entry URL fails closed
a declined row is REPORTED, not silently absent
a triple no row targets yields no plans
a multi-triple row plans once per triple, keyed on each
--engine selects a GROUP
--engine on an absent group is a structural error
the plan's allow-list carries the row's own hosts - upstream AND corroboration
a host from ANOTHER manifest row is not on this group's allow-list
a compiled group is ONE plan holding every source, not one plan per source
the entry is `.src`-keyed, which stage-engines structurally cannot match
each source is verified against its OWN from_source.tarball_sha256
each source carries the detached signature url its row declares
the two sources are the two DIFFERENT urls of the one compiled group
the plan's allow-list carries the row's own hosts - upstream, signature AND corroboration
a from-source row is invisible to the PREBUILT planner
a PREBUILT row is invisible to the SOURCE planner
a from-source row this triple does not target yields no source plan
a from-source SUB-COMPONENT is not a source plan - only staged artifacts compile
two rows sharing ONE source fetch it once
a from-source row with no tarball anchor is refused, not silently skipped
a from-source row that cannot LOCATE its signature is refused
a `from_source` that is not a table is refused, not read as an empty one
two sources whose urls share a filename are refused, not silently overwritten
a source url with no usable filename is refused
a group resolving to two source entry names fails closed
the entry holds the RAW archive bytes - the signature is over the archive as shipped, so nothing is unpacked
a multi-source group publishes EVERY source; none is discarded
each detached signature is published beside its own archive
the entry holds exactly the declared sources and their signatures, nothing else
a source whose bytes miss the pin is refused, and NOTHING is published
a malformed SOURCE pin names the from-source key, not the prebuilt one
the source fetch is bound by the plan's OWN allow-list
the SIGNATURE fetch is bound by the allow-list too, not only the tarball fetch
a source url whose tail is drive-relative is refused - it would escape the entry
a url tail that is a multi-SEGMENT name is refused
a SIGNATURE url whose tail is drive-relative is refused on the same grammar
the publish refuses to hand over an entry that is not what the plan declares
a stray NON-directory at the entry path is never mistaken for a benign race
a concurrent publish is counted as a HIT in the --source summary
a concurrently-published entry reports THAT, not a fabricated populate
run(sources=True) reaches the SOURCE path - a `.src` entry, not a prebuilt one
run() WITHOUT --source populates nothing here - the two modes are disjoint
main --source threads the mode through to the SOURCE path
main WITHOUT --source finds no PREBUILT row in the same manifest
a from-source cache HIT is reported under -v
the --source summary counts a HIT as a hit, not as work still to do
the PREBUILT summary counts a HIT the same way - the arithmetic is one class
a populated source entry is a cache HIT, not a second download
an absent entry plans as a MISS
populate publishes the entry under the stage-engines key
a published entry plans as a HIT
no staging residue survives a success
a hash mismatch refuses to publish, AS a mismatch
a refused populate leaves the cache EMPTY
a concurrent publish is reported as such, NOT as a populate of ours
the concurrently-published entry is left INTACT and ours leaves no residue
a stray NON-directory at the entry path is never mistaken for a benign race
...and it either becomes the verified tree or is left untouched by a loud failure
a hash-VALID but traversing archive is still refused AS a traversal
the refused traversing archive left no entry and no residue
an empty manifest is a no-op run
an empty manifest run creates no cache directory
--check fetches nothing
--check creates no cache directory either
a full run populates the entry
a second run is a pure cache hit - the opener is never called
run() REPORTS a concurrent publish rather than letting it escape
a triple with no row is a no-op, not an error
main() refuses neither --engine nor --all
main() refuses BOTH --engine and --all
a missing manifest is a structural error
